{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1410200-the-lie-and-the-nature-of-the-universe","id":1410200,"title":"The Lie and the Nature of the Universe","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-24T20:07:54-07:00","id":1410200,"title":"The Lie and the Nature of the Universe","content":"I think the nature of reality in Mage changes over time as people develop technology. The more people develop technology the more elaborate the Lie has to get.<br /> <br /> Maybe the earth really was the center of the universe once with planets moving around it. Is that a secret reason why the church/people has a strong aversion to new technology and science? Is that what causes the cognitive dissonance some experience when new evidence contradicts their world view? Do people come to the edge of understanding and experience Paradox instead of an Awakening?<br /> <br /> It could explain why fewer people Awaken now. There's fewer mysteries to trigger enlightenment about reality, because the Lie has become so exhaustive.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25825-fuguestate","name":"FugueState","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25825_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T22:26:13-07:00","id":1410227,"title":"","content":"\u2026Not really?<br /> <br /> Exposure to the supernatural prompts breaking points for most people with Integrity, which is the mechanical face of &quot;people in this setting all kind of already know, in broad terms, that there's monsters in the dark, and they're not eager to talk about it for various reasons.&quot; The Lie is the world those people pretend they inhabit with this denial, not any sort of deeper nature of reality that's constantly being revised in a way that player-level characters need to worry about.<br /> <br /> Awakenings being less common over time has never been anything more concrete than rhetoric. The Awakened have something of a cultural bad habit of telling themselves that they ought to be even more powerful and influential but reality won't let them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T22:46:43-07:00","id":1410230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FugueState</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1410200-the-lie-and-the-nature-of-the-universe#post1410200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the nature of reality in Mage changes over time as people develop technology. The more people develop technology the more elaborate the Lie has to get.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is pretty explicitly not how it works, that's how <i>Mage: the Ascension</i> works.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe the earth really was the center of the universe once with planets moving around it. Is that a secret reason why the church/people has a strong aversion to new technology and science? </div> </div> </div>Historically the Catholic Church has actually been instrumental in the advancement of science, and even the Gallileo affair had more to do with Gallileo being an asshat than the Church flat out rejecting the heliocentric model. It has only been with the rise of right-wing religious fundamentalism that some religious groups have been anti-science.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is that what causes the cognitive dissonance some experience when new evidence contradicts their world view? Do people come to the edge of understanding and experience Paradox instead of an Awakening? </div> </div> </div>People can, and obviously <i>do</i>, experience things without a supernatural explanation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It could explain why fewer people Awaken now. </div> </div> </div>[citation needed]<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's fewer mysteries to trigger enlightenment about reality, because the Lie has become so exhaustive. </div> </div> </div>[citation needed]<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thoughts? </div> </div> </div>Your ideas do not really mesh with <i>Awakening</i>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T23:04:41-07:00","id":1410233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1410200-the-lie-and-the-nature-of-the-universe?p=1410230#post1410230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is pretty explicitly not how it works, that's how <i>Mage: the Ascension</i> works.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Historically the Catholic Church has actually been instrumental in the advancement of science, and even the Gallileo affair had more to do with Gallileo being an asshat than the Church flat out rejecting the heliocentric model. It has only been with the rise of right-wing religious fundamentalism that some religious groups have been anti-science.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> People can, and obviously <i>do</i>, experience things without a supernatural explanation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> [citation needed]<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> [citation needed]<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Your ideas do not really mesh with <i>Awakening</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>If i remember well in dark eras it is explained that the Awakenings were more frequent, but the less raw number of people resulted in 2-3 mages fir village at most.<br /> It also state that awakenings were harsher and more often lethals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T07:06:48-07:00","id":1410283,"title":"","content":"I think you'd need to elaborate this a bit more; you haven't really given a reason why science/technology would require elaborating the Lie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T07:35:28-07:00","id":1410286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1410200-the-lie-and-the-nature-of-the-universe?p=1410233#post1410233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If i remember well in dark eras it is explained that the Awakenings were more frequent, but the less raw number of people resulted in 2-3 mages fir village at most.<br /> It also state that awakenings were harsher and more often lethals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if there were less people in the world, it makes sense that there were less mages as well?<br /> <br /> It needs to be noted that the Watchtowers (which are more or less what connects the human soul to the Supernal truth) have &quot;grew&quot; togetehr with humanity (or at least, humanity's ability to understand the Supernal did, as in Sundered World there were very few of those), but with the exception of stating that humanity developing better scientific tools to know the truth is equivilent with humanity having a better understanding of the Truth (that is, Supernal Truth), which is more or less the Free Council's view of reality, there isn't really a connection between science and Supernal Magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T09:23:53-07:00","id":1410314,"title":"","content":"So, I decided to read through Dark Eras to find the [citation needed] stuff.<br /> <br /> re: Mysteries: the sidebar on page 47 titled &quot;Fading Wonders&quot; is clear that the reason there are fewer Time Before Mysteries is not because of science, but because of the constant Sleeper induced Dissonance eroding them away.<br /> <br /> re: Awakening: page 50, Neolithic Awakenings. Higher rate of Awakening, higher fatality rate, fewer overall Mages. There is no reason to believe this has anything to do with technology strengthening the Lie; it is more likely that Awakenings are less common per capita because of something like people being less likely to be forced into dire circumstances in more modern eras; less likely to encounter grand Mysteries because Sleeper Dissonance has eroded them away; or the Watchtowers themselves having a limited bandwidth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 08-25-2020, 12:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T18:39:13-07:00","id":1410434,"title":"","content":"So first, like proindrakenzoi said, Dark Eras is pretty explicit about there being proportionately more mages, and if you think about it, there would have to be for there to be a mage society. If only 1 in 10,000 people Awakens and there's only a few hundred thousand *people,* you have only a few mages at all, and you have no basis for mage society.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure the Neolithic and the Dark Era about Alexander the Great both talk about a decline in mages proportionate to the general population. But that's not really the focus of my position.<br /> <br /> When you lie, you have to keep track of your lies. As complications come up, your lie has to get more and more elaborate. The Lie gets pretty elaborate immediately. In the Neolithic Dark Era there are huge landscapes filled with stuff like broken time, where you can leave an area before you entered, and fate storms. They are supernatural disasters from the Time Before. And the Lie gradually smooths out reality. Eventually humans will conclude they evolved from apes and evidence of their magical origins disappears (as a 2e book Atlantis isn't emphasized).<br /> <br /> So the Lie isn't *simply* that magic doesn't exist. It's sort of a story that the material world tells about itself and tells us. There's no evidence of the Time Before except that there were some survivors who passed down stories. But we know there was a Time Before, from several different peoples. We know there's a point where even Time magic can't see our past. The Lie is a cover-up for a lot of things.<br /> <br /> So when people advance technology to see how light works, the Lie has to have an answer. So reality gets more detailed. That make sense?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25825-fuguestate","name":"FugueState","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25825_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T19:37:20-07:00","id":1410437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FugueState</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1410200-the-lie-and-the-nature-of-the-universe?p=1410434#post1410434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So first, like proindrakenzoi said, Dark Eras is pretty explicit about there being proportionately more mages, and if you think about it, there would have to be for there to be a mage society. If only 1 in 10,000 people Awakens and there's only a few hundred thousand *people,* you have only a few mages at all, and you have no basis for mage society.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure the Neolithic and the Dark Era about Alexander the Great both talk about a decline in mages proportionate to the general population. But that's not really the focus of my position.<br /> <br /> When you lie, you have to keep track of your lies. As complications come up, your lie has to get more and more elaborate. The Lie gets pretty elaborate immediately. In the Neolithic Dark Era there are huge landscapes filled with stuff like broken time, where you can leave an area before you entered, and fate storms. They are supernatural disasters from the Time Before. And the Lie gradually smooths out reality. Eventually humans will conclude they evolved from apes and evidence of their magical origins disappears (as a 2e book Atlantis isn't emphasized).<br /> <br /> So the Lie isn't *simply* that magic doesn't exist. It's sort of a story that the material world tells about itself and tells us. There's no evidence of the Time Before except that there were some survivors who passed down stories. But we know there was a Time Before, from several different peoples. We know there's a point where even Time magic can't see our past. The Lie is a cover-up for a lot of things.<br /> <br /> So when people advance technology to see how light works, the Lie has to have an answer. So reality gets more detailed. That make sense?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's dissonance. The case of disappearing signs of the supernal is what the Mysterium dubbed Pancryptia. All it does it get rid of supernal manifestations in the Fallen World. It does not add to it, only takes away<br /> <br /> And again, the Lie is almost nothing like Ascention. In ascention people explain how stuff works to get stuff like science. In Awakening, there is that which is Fallen and Supernal, with the Lie simply taking away the supernal (it the things like science were truly part of the Lie, then I dont think Techne would work)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 08-25-2020, 10:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T19:58:45-07:00","id":1410440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FugueState</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1410200-the-lie-and-the-nature-of-the-universe?p=1410434#post1410434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the Lie isn't *simply* that magic doesn't exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>The lexicon literally defines it as the force that tries to hide the truth of the Supernal World from Sleepers. A confrontation with it is required for an Awakening to kick off and Signs of Sorcery specifically gives encounters with supernatural creatures and glimpses of spells as examples of the sort of things that trigger the requisite Integrity breaking point roll that the Prospect in question exceptionally succeeds on.<br /> <br /> The Lie doesn't have to have an answer for how light works because, to paraphrase something Dave said a long time ago, light isn't made of magic; the Supernal <i>describes</i> Phenomenal reality, but Phenomenal reality is not intrinsically magical at the surface level the way the products of Supernal magic are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T20:32:03-07:00","id":1410441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FugueState</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1410200-the-lie-and-the-nature-of-the-universe?p=1410434#post1410434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you lie, you have to keep track of your lies. As complications come up, your lie has to get more and more elaborate. The Lie gets pretty elaborate immediately. In the Neolithic Dark Era there are huge landscapes filled with stuff like broken time, where you can leave an area before you entered, and fate storms. They are supernatural disasters from the Time Before. And the Lie gradually smooths out reality. Eventually humans will conclude they evolved from apes and evidence of their magical origins disappears (as a 2e book Atlantis isn't emphasized).<br /> <br /> So the Lie isn't *simply* that magic doesn't exist. It's sort of a story that the material world tells about itself and tells us. There's no evidence of the Time Before except that there were some survivors who passed down stories. But we know there was a Time Before, from several different peoples. We know there's a point where even Time magic can't see our past. The Lie is a cover-up for a lot of things.<br /> <br /> So when people advance technology to see how light works, the Lie has to have an answer. So reality gets more detailed. That make sense?</div> </div> </div> </div>Reality in Mage the Awakening is not created through perception. The Phenomenal World exists. It has a shape. It doesn't stop having that shape when you stop looking at it. If a tree falls in the woods and nobody is there to hear it, it still makes a sound. The world doesn't just exist for the benefit of the humans perceiving it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage the Awakening Second Edition p. 59</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like the lake, the world as most Sleepers know it is a Lie. The sea serpents under the ordinary-seeming lake are real, and most urban legends and horror movies reflect some aspect of the truth humanity wants to deny. This is not because human belief shapes reality but because the terrifying realities of the world quietly nudge human minds that would prefer not to believe in such things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plato's cave is the classic example for a reason. The Forms move before the fire and their shadows are cast on the wall. The Lie is the shackle that keeps the prisoners from rising to behold the Forms directly. To inspect the shadows more closely does not change the Forms.<br /> <br /> To be in thrall to the Lie is to look away from the truth and make excuses for not seeing it. It's not to hallucinate a false reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 08-25-2020, 11:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-26T08:37:08-07:00","id":1410522,"title":"","content":"To continue the demographic thread of the conversation: one of the metamorphic Awakenings in Signs of Sorcery only happens when two people Awaken to the same Watchtower simultaneously, which have only started happening often enough for Mage society to take notice relatively recently as the human population has boomed.<br /> <br /> As much as all demographic notes are suggestions, and you'll hopefully never get a Mage:Sleeper ratio like oVampire constantly makes the mistake of doing, the proportion of Mages to Sleepers has gone <i>down</i> over history, but the actual number of mages has gone <i>up</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-26T08:56:51-07:00","id":1410523,"title":"","content":"So does that mean that the Lie is more powerful in the present or that the growth in the number of Awakenings is proportionally slower than the population growth ? Perhaps both ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 08-26-2020, 12:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-26T09:48:11-07:00","id":1410526,"title":"","content":"This is a great thread. I find the theory behind the Lie absolutely fascinating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-26T09:49:27-07:00","id":1410527,"title":"","content":"But it is easy to get confused between the two Mage games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-26T12:05:19-07:00","id":1410540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1410200-the-lie-and-the-nature-of-the-universe?p=1410526#post1410526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a great thread. I find the theory behind the Lie absolutely fascinating.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, but some details still confunds me.<br /> For example i don t understand if it is possible to trick a sleeper into thinking that i am creating a fire with a lighter (which in truth is empty) while i am using a spell without incurring in a paradox","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-26T12:28:03-07:00","id":1410545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1410200-the-lie-and-the-nature-of-the-universe?p=1410523#post1410523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So does that mean that the Lie is more powerful in the present or that the growth in the number of Awakenings is proportionally slower than the population growth ? Perhaps both ?</div> </div> </div> </div>At least in one sense, we know that the Lie is more powerful; the Seers exist. Before them, the Exarchs were apparently happy to leave mages alone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-26T12:45:00-07:00","id":1410546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1410200-the-lie-and-the-nature-of-the-universe?p=1410540#post1410540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed, but some details still confunds me.<br /> For example i don t understand if it is possible to trick a sleeper into thinking that i am creating a fire with a lighter (which in truth is empty) while i am using a spell without incurring in a paradox</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage the Awakening Second Edition p. 298</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Curse strikes a Sleeper when she sees obvious magic, either during the spell\u2019s casting or encountering its effects later. So what\u2019s obvious? The spell must be clearly, openly supernatural in effect, and the Sleeper must be both conscious and cognizant of the magic\u2019s impossibility. Spells that are not obvious at the moment they are cast escape the Paradox die bonus, but may be subject to Dissonance if they are obvious when a Sleeper later encounters them.</div> </div> </div> </div>So if you're casting a spell in such a way that is visually indistinguishable from a nonmagical action to the witness's limited knowledge \u2013 the sleeper doesn't know the lighter is empty, you're flicking the strike, and you're not employing any obviously occult yantras to aid your spellcasting \u2013 then a sleeper witness won't risk a Paradox.<br /> <br /> If you do employ obviously occult yantras, chant the High Speech, or the sleeper knows the lighter is empty and flicking the strike will not ignite a flame, any potential resulting Paradox isn't the result of the sleeper not believing what happens. It's the result of the Sleeping Curse. The sleeper is spriritually, metaphysically incapable of acknowledging the direct intercession of supernal truth; to look directly into the sacred light is blinding. The only way for the sleeper's soul to shield itself from total truth is to touch untruth, and in doing so, brush against the Abyss. A Paradox is an invasion into the Supernal World of the anti-truths of the Abyss, the set of impossibilities and contradictions. Paradoxes twist the spell-form which supernal symbols take in the Phenomenal World and cause shearing anomalies that warp causality and reason.<br /> <br /> The same thing doesn't happen if a vampire or a ghostly revenant does impossible things before the sleeper's eyes. In both cases, the sleeper suffers a shock to her Integrity from what is a bizarre, uncanny, and often terrifying (given the circumstances in which this usually happens) event. Sleepers in the Chronicles of Darkness often block out or rationalize these memories, or find some other way to pretend they never happened so as to avoid facing the terror of their deeper implications. But an intruding Paradox is invited by the <i>spiritual</i> shock of staring supernal truth in the face, which is felt even though the sleeper cannot consciously distinguish a supernal spell of teleportation from a demon exploiting spatial folds.<br /> <br /> Supernal sorcery calls to the human soul. A soul in the grip of the Lie cannot bear to hear it. Their spirit fractures ever slightly, and the outer chaos rushes in through the crack.<br /> <br /> Supernal sorcery strips the world bare. Eyes shaded by the Lie bleed to see it. The tears they shed come from the Abyss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 08-26-2020, 03:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-26T12:47:12-07:00","id":1410548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1410200-the-lie-and-the-nature-of-the-universe?p=1410545#post1410545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At least in one sense, we know that the Lie is more powerful; the Seers exist. Before them, the Exarchs were apparently happy to leave mages alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Seers are a direct reaction to Mages organizing into Orders. The Exarchs didn't &quot;leave mages alone&quot; before then, they just used isolated agents because there was no need to have their own organizations to counter the unorganized Wise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-26T14:22:21-07:00","id":1410565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1410200-the-lie-and-the-nature-of-the-universe?p=1410548#post1410548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Seers are a direct reaction to Mages organizing into Orders.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, that's the point I'm driving at. You now have a global organisation of Awakened actively reinforcing the Lie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-26T14:54:55-07:00","id":1410571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1410200-the-lie-and-the-nature-of-the-universe?p=1410565#post1410565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know, that's the point I'm driving at. You now have a global organisation of Awakened actively reinforcing the Lie.</div> </div> </div> </div>You ignored the second part: &quot;The Exarchs didn't &quot;leave mages alone&quot; before then, they just used isolated agents because there was no need to have their own organizations to counter the unorganized Wise.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Seers don't represent the Lie weighing more heavily on the world, in many ways they represent the opposite: those fighting for Truth have become stronger, requiring those trying to preserve the Lie to engage in more active measures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-26T15:16:34-07:00","id":1410574,"title":"","content":"Plus it's not as if there aren't humans entirely willing to push the Exarch agenda without knowing it. You don't need to be Awakened to be a tyrant or crush the souls of your fellow human. You may not get Resources 8, but for a lot of the world Resources 3 is enough of a reward.<br /> <br /> Advances in technology seems like it would be more likely to cause the rise and fall of ministries rather than put any undue stress on the Lie. Like Panopticon is such a popular idea it's almost instantly recognizable and only seems to grow more powerful with technology, while Phemian could mean anything or nothing at all and probably doesn't rely on the same 'control through surveillance' idea that has become easier and more widespread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-26-2020, 06:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}